  {
   "kind": "interpretation",
   "title": "Explanation and interpretation",
   "sort_order": 9,
   "payload": {
    "sections": [
     {
      "heading": "Question",
      "paragraphs": [
       "Is severe disease a larger cytokine perturbation (size), or a shift in the balance of the response (MCP-1 relative to IL-8) at a similar size?"
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "What was done",
      "paragraphs": [
       "For each infected dog: the number of the 6 shared analytes outside its own file's healthy-control range (perturbation count), and the within-file percentile of MCP-1 minus that of IL-8 (balance index). Each was compared between severe and non-severe dogs with Cliff's delta (bootstrap CI by dog, permutation p, BH within each file, family of 2). Sensitivities: a z-score version for analytes with under 20% floor values, counts above and below the range separately, and floors at half the floor."
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "Result",
      "paragraphs": [
       "S-CB050 (B. rossi, died 12 vs survived 85): perturbation +0.04 (-0.22 to +0.31), mean 1.42 vs 1.38 analytes; balance +0.32 (+0.02 to +0.60), permutation p 0.070, q 0.139.",
       "S-CB017 (B. canis, complicated 18 vs uncomplicated 13): perturbation +0.71 (+0.43 to +0.92), mean 4.11 vs 2.69, q < 0.001; balance +0.44 (+0.07 to +0.78), q 0.038.",
       "Verdict by the pre-stated rule: balance. The balance shift has the same sign in both files, but in S-CB050 it is weak (the bootstrap interval only just excludes 0 and the permutation p is 0.070). It is carried by MCP-1, which is higher in severe dogs in both files; IL-8 itself does not differ (experiment SV-04-01). In B. canis, complicated dogs also have a larger perturbation, so size and balance both hold there; in B. rossi, dogs that died do not have more analytes out of range. 2 of 4 tests passed q < 0.05."
      ]
     },
     {
      "heading": "What this does not show",
      "paragraphs": [
       "The balance index is a rank difference of two analytes; it is not a validated measure of immune balance, and MCP-1 drives most of it here.",
       "Control ranges come from 15 and 16 dogs, so 'outside the range' is a coarse threshold. S-CB017 controls include dogs given prophylactic imidocarb (inferred from the ID prefix).",
       "The 'complicated' label of S-CB017 is defined partly by inflammation (SIRS), so a larger perturbation there is partly built into the label.",
       "One species per source: the difference between files (size in B. canis, not in B. rossi) cannot be attributed to species. Died includes euthanasia for poor prognosis. Descriptive re-analysis."
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  }
